{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/955221-why-the-exarchs-truly-ascended-a-non-canon-perspective","id":955221,"title":"Why the Exarchs truly Ascended (a non-canon perspective)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T15:17:28-07:00","id":955221,"title":"Why the Exarchs truly Ascended (a non-canon perspective)","content":"Alright, so I created a different viewpoint in my game for why the Exarchs chose to Ascend, and why the World remains &quot;Fallen&quot;.<br /> <br /> For a long time, it was accepted that the Exarchs chose to enter the Celestial Ladder to become God-Kings, seperate from the mortal coil and its trappings. That they committed the single greatest act of Hubris to date. There are, however, dissenters to that belief. No, not the Seers, who believe a sycophantic existence is better than being a magical equivalent to a guerilla fighter. No, this view supposes that the Exarchs chose to enter on the belief they would SAVE the world, not control it. They devised the Ladder at a point in history when humanity was in danger, and they thought entering this new frequency could allow them to restore peace to their existence.<br /> <br /> Magic was rampant and in the hand of tyrants and saints alike. Their machinations were close to ripping the world into shards that nothing could ever grow from again. So in their Hubris, they devised the Watchtowers; intelligent engines of magic designed to locate and test new aspirants to magic, allowing them a chance to join the fold. They, however, did not know what would come of this action. They rose only to find a hole left in their wake, from which the Abyss leaked through. They didn't know that would happen, did they? Did they just accept and roll with it? Does this mean the Exarchs and Oracles are the same? If so, then what do Tetrarchs talk to? Have they been corrupted into nothing more than Symbols of the very things they wanted to prevent, their original selves washed away in the power of the raw Supernal? <br /> <br /> What do you guys think? I find it to be a fresh, less popular view on the how and why things are the way they are, with questions, conjecture, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:03:57-07:00","id":955333,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to find the original part. As far as I can tell it's the bit where the Exarchs were trying to save the world and the bit about the Watchtowers being magical engines.<br /> <br /> There's actually a number of Seers and members of the Pentacle who do believe that the Exarchs and the Oracles are either essentially the same, or in fact the same. You can read about it in the Seer book from 1e. Since the Exarchs don't bother to explain themselves there's already a lot of speculation on what their true motives are, and why they've done what they've done and how their Ascension might have changed them and/or their agendas.<br /> <br /> Maybe I missed something though. Do you think you can clarify where the fresh, hot take is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:32:54-07:00","id":955363,"title":"","content":"I guess it's better to clarify that I consider this a fresh take for me, as opposed to in general. I never read Seers of the Throne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:43:34-07:00","id":955365,"title":"","content":"It's tricky to make relevant to the players unless you want to go the full Atlantean Rock Opera* route with visions of old, conversations with beings who were around for the Fall, and the like.<br /> <br /> *My phrase. I'm not sure the fandom has picked a consistent phrase for this kind of game, which I enjoy as a guilty pleasure despite what it does to the default assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:48:31-07:00","id":955368,"title":"","content":"I created this without considering Atlantis as it was portrayed in 1E. I just went with a general idea that could anyway you see fit, even if it's just background dressing for some NPC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:20:59-07:00","id":955597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/955221-why-the-exarchs-truly-ascended-a-non-canon-perspective?p=955365#post955365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's tricky to make relevant to the players unless you want to go the full Atlantean Rock Opera* route with visions of old, conversations with beings who were around for the Fall, and the like.<br /> <br /> *My phrase. I'm not sure the fandom has picked a consistent phrase for this kind of game, which I enjoy as a guilty pleasure despite what it does to the default assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god, Atlantean Rock Opera is a <i>great</i> name for a certain kind of Mage game. I love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:43:08-07:00","id":955612,"title":"","content":"I like things like this to float around in the setting, mostly because various attempts at making Seers of the Throne ideology and goals look less sinister and less evil always strived me as a natural thing for Seers to do. It doesn't matter, for me, if they are actually right or if they are forging another Lie to let themselves sleep at night.<br /> A similar thing I like to throw around is<br /> &quot;You people always seem to assume that Exarchs are reason for everything that's wrong with this world, and that without them, everything would revert to the previous and long-lost state of paradise. But how do you know that? How do you know that the world before Exarchs was better? What if it was even worse, and it's their doing that allows at least some to be happy? <br /> You want everyone to be always happy. GROW UP. We are trying. We are trying hard. We are working, we are making sacrifices. What are YOU doing, other than complaining and disturbing the world around you?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:59:54-07:00","id":955948,"title":"","content":"Yeah WHW has a good idea here. How do we know what kind of world the Old Gods ran anyway? It was not human centric for sure and may have been very hostile. Atlantis may have been run by mages but mages may have just been pawns to some other power. The only hope of overthrowing that power may have been to take a risk and empower a select group to overthrow the Old Gods. The fact that the exarchs chose to slam the door behind them afterward may have been selfish but a risk people were desperate enough to take. And the Abyss? Who knows what would have happened to reality if the Gate hadn't sacrificed its place in the supernal to tame the darkness. Maybe the Abyss keeps the lower depths from consuming reality. I don't personally favor this interpretation but something like it is probably what the most devout seers believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:36:22-07:00","id":956404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/955221-why-the-exarchs-truly-ascended-a-non-canon-perspective?p=955612#post955612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like things like this to float around in the setting, mostly because various attempts at making Seers of the Throne ideology and goals look less sinister and less evil always strived me as a natural thing for Seers to do. It doesn't matter, for me, if they are actually right or if they are forging another Lie to let themselves sleep at night.<br /> A similar thing I like to throw around is<br /> &quot;You people always seem to assume that Exarchs are reason for everything that's wrong with this world, and that without them, everything would revert to the previous and long-lost state of paradise. But how do you know that? How do you know that the world before Exarchs was better? What if it was even worse, and it's their doing that allows at least some to be happy?<br /> You want everyone to be always happy. GROW UP. We are trying. We are trying hard. We are working, we are making sacrifices. What are YOU doing, other than complaining and disturbing the world around you?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My thoughts exactly. What differs between both worlds? Not much, according to this philosophy. Even with magic, there was pain, death, disease. The Abyss wasn't around to clog the Underworld or help speed up the Sundering sure, but was it ever any simpler? We cannot be certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}